WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.680
What to show in your portfolio, and why.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.230
This is the video for module one of Online Portfolio Building.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.920
When you tell someone, I am a good tailor, you are asking them to trust your word.

4
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:21.400
When you show them five finished pieces, each with a short story of what the customer needed, they can judge for themselves.

5
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:29.820
An online portfolio is one place on the internet, reached with one link, where you show your best work with that story.

6
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:37.290
It works for you while you sleep. A WhatsApp status is different: it disappears after 24 hours.

7
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.260
Think of the busy person opening your link. She quietly asks four questions.

8
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.830
First, can she do what I need? She looks for work similar to her own job.

9
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.140
Second, is the quality good enough? She looks closely at photos, finishing and detail.

10
00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:01.790
Third, can I trust her? She looks for real customers, results, testimonials, and a real name and face.

11
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:09.800
Fourth, how do I reach her, and what will it cost? She looks for a clear contact button and a guide to your prices.

12
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:13.840
Your portfolio should answer all four without her needing to ask you.

13
00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:23.050
For example, Ngozi is a tailor in Enugu. A new customer wants to see her work before ordering an aso ebi outfit.

14
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:32.490
First, Ngozi forwards 37 photos in one message. Some are blurry, some are not hers, and none say what the customer asked for.

15
00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:45.300
Then Ngozi sends one link to a simple free website with six pieces. Each has three clear photos, front, back and the beading detail, and four short lines about the job.

16
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:51.050
The customer messages her with the exact style she likes. The portfolio did the selling.

17
00:01:52.300 --> 00:02:03.350
Before you choose anything, write one sentence. Who is your portfolio for, and what should they do? For example, mothers planning children's parties who should message me to order a cake.

18
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:16.030
Next, remove anything that is not your own work. Never use photos from Pinterest or a supplier's catalogue. Customers find out, and one copy can destroy all your trust.

19
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:24.300
Then test each piece twice. Quality: is this among my best? Relevance: does it match the work I want more of?

20
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:33.100
Show range within your focus. Different occasions, sizes, budgets or colours tell the viewer you can handle her job.

21
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:41.180
Put your strongest, most relevant piece first, and your second strongest last, because people remember endings.

22
00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:49.790
The most common mistake is showing too much. A viewer remembers your weakest three pieces, so keep five to eight strong ones.

23
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:59.830
For example, Amaka bakes cakes in Abuja. Her goal is mothers planning children's birthday parties. She starts with 40 cake photos.

24
00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:09.630
She removes 9 photos that are blurry or taken at night under yellow bulbs, then 7 that are other bakers' cakes saved for ideas.

25
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:18.540
She scores her 14 children's cakes from 1 to 5, and keeps the five that score 4 or 5, each with a different theme.

26
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:26.490
She adds one cupcake box, because mothers often order cupcakes too. Six strong, relevant pieces.

27
00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:41.890
A portfolio is public, so protect your customers and yourself. Ask permission before you show a customer's face, name, home or event. A WhatsApp message is enough. Save the reply in a Permissions folder.

28
00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:55.490
Check every photo for phone numbers, addresses and receipts. Never show a child's face without the parent's clear permission. Never post your BVN, NIN, bank login or ID card.

29
00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:07.400
Show your area, like Surulere, Lagos, not your full address. And label honestly. If you worked in a team, name your part. If it was practice, say practice project.

30
00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:14.840
To remember. A portfolio shows proof, not claims. Answer the four questions every viewer asks.

31
00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:24.340
Choose five to eight strong, relevant pieces, best first. Show only your own work, labelled honestly. And protect privacy before you publish.

32
00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:37.110
Now it is your turn. Write your one-sentence goal, shortlist your pieces, set up one tidy folder with a Permissions sub-folder, and send permission messages to two customers.

33
00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.400
Continue with the lessons below.
